    "summary": "Smokin' Greek Theatre ’82 – tight set, rippin’ Deal solo & stellar Jack Straw",
    "review": "The May 22, 1982 Greek Theatre show is a textbook example of the early‑‘80s Dead firing on all cylinders. From the opening “Jack Straw” that snaps you awake to the high‑octane first set – “Sugaree”, “Cassidy”, “Tennessee Jed” (with a story‑like solo) and the monster “Lazy Lightning > Supplication” – the band rides a wave of pure energy that never quits. The second set delivers one of the most satisfying “China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider” pairs of the era, a tight “Man Smart, Woman Smarter”, a soulful Brent‑led “Never Trust A Woman (Good Times Blues)”, and an inspired “Not Fade Away” jam that rolls into a soaring “Wharf Rat”. Highlights also include a rippin’ “Deal” solo that fans still talk about. All of this is captured in crystal‑clear soundboard quality, making the Greek run feel both intimate and epic.\n\nThe Miller SBD (gd1982-05-22.sbd.miller.96331.sbeok.flac16) stands out as the definitive source – its pristine mix lets every nuance shine, from Jerry’s scorching lead to Phil’s crystal‑clear bass and Brent’s soulful keys. Whether you’re a completist or just after one of the best snapshots of the Dead in ’82, this recording delivers the full, high‑energy experience without drops or hiss.",
